  "worked_solution": "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(12{x}^{2}-24x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -8 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(4{c}^{3}-12{c}^{2}+c)-0] \\\\ -8 & =4{c}^{2}-12c+1 \\\\ 0 & =4{c}^{2}-12c+9 \\\\ 0 & =(2c-3)^{2} \\\\ c & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$",
